<h1 class="docs-title">Blazor.Map</h1>
<p class="docs-lede">A Blazor component library for interactive maps powered by MapLibre GL JS.</p>

<div class="docs-meta-row">
    <span class="docs-chip">MIT licensed</span>
    <span class="docs-chip"><code>net10.0</code></span>
    <span class="docs-chip">MapLibre GL JS</span>
</div>

<p><a href="installation">Get started</a> with the installation guide, or <a href="components/sgb-map">see the examples</a>.</p>

<h2 id="features">Features</h2>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Vector and raster tiles</strong>: OpenFreeMap presets work out of the box with no API key. Also supports WMS, WMTS, ArcGIS MapServer, and any custom MapLibre style URL.</li>
    <li><strong>Markers and shapes</strong>: DOM-based markers with drag support, GPU-rendered circles and polylines, and programmatic or marker-anchored popups.</li>
    <li><strong>Real-time tracking</strong>: <code>TrackedEntityLayer</code> manages moving entities with smooth updates, path decorations, and built-in clustering.</li>
    <li><strong>Style composition</strong>: compose multiple MapLibre styles. Layer a base map with one or more overlay styles, each with their own sources and layers.</li>
    <li><strong>Interactive legends</strong>: toggleable legend control with fully customisable item templates, wired to layer visibility groups.</li>
    <li><strong>Dark mode</strong>: light and dark themes for UI controls, navigation, scale bar, popups, and attribution, independent of map tile styling.</li>
</ul>
